algorithms.pseudocode:
function NORMALIZE(t, rules):
    repeat:
        for each subterm s of t (bottom-up):
            for each rule r in rules:
                if r matches s:
                    replace s with r(s) in t
                    break
    until no rule fires
    return t

Complexity: O(max_steps * |rules| * depth(t))
Termination: Guaranteed for convergent systems

function SATURATE(egraph, rules, max_iters):
    repeat:
        new_merges = 0
        for each term t in egraph:
            for each rule r:
                if r matches t:
                    result = apply(r, t)
                    merge(id(t), add(result))
                    new_merges += 1
    until new_merges == 0 or iters > max_iters

Complexity: O(iters * |terms| * |rules|)

function EXTRACT(egraph, class_id, cost_fn):
    root = find(class_id)
    best = argmin { cost_fn(t) : find(id(t)) == root }
    return best

Complexity: O(|egraph|)
Correctness: By Theorem 3, eval(EXTRACT(t)) = eval(t)
